# This is a list of GPIO pins, set by the script /etc/init.d/gpio_pins.sh
# They are documented at: https://github.com/victronenergy/venus/wiki/bbb-gpio
# Format: <pin_number> <direction: in/out> <name>
#
# The <name> part is used to create a symlink in /dev/gpio.
#
# Pin numbers are GLOBAL sysfs gpio numbers, not BCM/header numbers -
# see the raspberrypi4-64 gpio_list (same pin policy, same kernel
# recipe/version as this board) for why. NOT independently verified on
# real raspberrypi5 hardware - inferring the same gpiochip0 base of
# 512 since this board shares the exact same kernel recipe/version
# (linux-raspberrypi 6.12.25-rpi-venus-2) as raspberrypi4-64, just a
# different defconfig (bcm2712 vs bcm2711). Confirm against
# /sys/class/gpio/gpiochip0 (or whichever chip0 directory actually
# appears) before relying on this in the field.
#
# Pin choices avoid GPIO 16/17/18, which the spi1-3cs overlay (used for
# a dual-channel CAN HAT in Dual SPI mode - standard on GX devices)
# claims as dedicated chip-select lines. Digital input 4 and relay 1
# use the alternate assignments from kwindrem/RpiGpioSetup's
# gpio_listForCanHats for the same reason; relay 2 and the 5th digital
# input from that reference list were dropped rather than reassigned
# to keep this default minimal - edit this file directly for anything
# else.
#
# Digital inputs need a pull-up that isn't the chip default outside
# GPIO 1-8 - see the paired venus-gpio-pullups-overlay.dts overlay.

# relays are active HIGH
# Relay 1   BCM GPIO 2  (512+2=514)  header pin 3  (alternate assignment, avoids i2c0/i2c1)
514 out relay_1
# Relay 2   BCM GPIO 27 (512+27=539) header pin 13
539 out relay_2

# Digital input 1   BCM GPIO 5  (512+5=517)  header pin 29
517 in digital_input_1
# Digital input 2   BCM GPIO 6  (512+6=518)  header pin 31
518 in digital_input_2
# Digital input 3   BCM GPIO 13 (512+13=525) header pin 33
525 in digital_input_3
# Digital input 4   BCM GPIO 3  (512+3=515)  header pin 5  (alternate assignment)
515 in digital_input_4
